WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.540
A charge is written above a
cross: The King of the Jews.

2
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.360
It is meant as mockery.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.270
Passers-by jeer.

4
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.250
The chief priests say: He saved others.

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.040
He can't save himself.

6
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:17.300
From noon to 3 in the afternoon,
darkness covers the land.

7
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.220
Then a loud cry, and death.

8
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:25.570
Then the Roman centurion in charge of
the execution calls him Son of God.

9
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.880
Why would a Roman officer, of all people,

10
00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.380
say that here?

11
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.230
In this mission, you'll
read the cry from the cross,

12
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.040
and see why a Temple curtain
tears from top to bottom.

13
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.360
Then you'll explore how different
Christians explain why Jesus died.

14
00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:45.870
Your mission: explain why a Roman soldier's
words matter so much in Mark's account.
